    "created_at": "2016-10-27T01:57:31Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-10-27T01:57:31Z",
    "body": "Yeah, that was my thinking too.  Malte makes a good point that this is probably mainly useful cross-document (because within a single document there's no security boundary - just like `Event.isTrusted`).  \n\nBut I can imagine some scenarios where it's useful to know even within a document.  For example, you want to do a window.open either directly or (if you can tell it'll get blocked) via some additional \"click here to open\" UI.\n",
