    "created_at": "2016-10-27T03:12:12Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-10-27T03:12:12Z",
    "body": "I have no preference in API really. If we can make it work for `setTimeout` and friends that is cool, of course.\n\nExposing this will unlock a lot of use cases. For example it is rarely possible to use `sandbox` on iframe today without allowing `allow-popups` and `allow-top-navigation`. If user gestures were exposed, one could mandate to iframes: \"Let me know when you would like to navigate via a message\" and then the container can, for example, check whether the destination is acceptable, before executing the navigation on behalf of the child iframe.\n\nIn AMP we'd like to allow iframes to request resize in response to a user gesture, which is very similar.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
