    "created_at": "2017-06-15T16:44:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-06-15T16:44:19Z",
    "body": "The difficult thing about audio playback is that while AudioContext works for a lot of things, it is designed around fully-decoded, fully-decompressed audio buffers. This is unsuitable for long music tracks, where HTMLAudioElement has a nice streaming capability. However being a DOM element it's difficult to see how it would ever run in a worker. Perhaps one day MediaStreams will even be transferrable to a worker, but even then you still need a play() call on a DOM element that would have to obey user gesture restrictions.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
